.TH GIT-REMOTE-KEYBASE 1
.SH NAME
git-remote-keybase \- daemonless Git transport for encrypted Keybase repositories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git-remote-keybase
[options] remote [keybase://type/folder/repository]
.br
.B git-remote-keybase --setup --username USER --device-name NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Git invokes this helper for keybase:// URLs.
It uses the official Keybase cryptographic and KBFS implementations in process.
No Keybase daemon, KBFS daemon, mount or Homebrew service is required.
Capability negotiation does not open an authenticated session.
.PP
Configure the account once with:
.br
.B git config --global keybase.username USER
.PP
Command-line --username takes precedence over KEYBASE_GIT_USERNAME, which takes
precedence over Git's keybase.username setting.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
The default auto mode uses a configured helper device, otherwise it reads
existing official-client device credentials without modifying them.
If those credentials no longer exist, --setup authorizes a dedicated device
once using a Paper Key. Its device name is public.
Encrypted device keys and the macOS Keychain unlock material are retained.
The Paper Key itself is not stored.
.PP
--auth-mode accepts auto, existing, device or oneshot.
The oneshot mode is an explicit temporary Paper Key session.
--paper-key-fd accepts an inherited descriptor of at least 3, only for setup
or oneshot mode. It must be closed by its writer after supplying the key.
.SH FILES
Persistent devices are stored under the user's configuration directory,
keybase-git-standalone/devices/USER.
Identity caches for borrowed devices are stored under the user's cache directory,
keybase-git-standalone/identities.
These directories and the system Keychain are outside the Homebrew Cellar.
Package upgrades and uninstall do not remove or revoke devices.
.PP
KEYBASE_GIT_STATE_DIR and KEYBASE_GIT_CACHE_DIR override their parent directories.
KEYBASE_GIT_KEYBASE_HOME selects an existing official-client home.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
--version prints helper and Keybase versions.
--diagnostics reports initialization timing and, for long-running requests,
symbolic goroutine stacks without argument values.
.SH SEE ALSO
git(1), git-config(1), gitremote-helpers(7), brew(1)
